**Irish History Summary (2 sentences):**

Ireland's history spans from prehistoric settlements around 10,500 BC through Celtic, Viking, and Norman periods, followed by over 800 years of English and British political and military involvement beginning with the Norman invasion of 1169, marked by recurring conflicts, rebellions, and the devastating Great Famine of 1845-1852. After centuries of struggle for independence, Ireland was partitioned in 1922 into the Irish Free State (later the Republic of Ireland) comprising 26 counties and Northern Ireland (6 counties remaining in the UK), with the latter experiencing decades of sectarian conflict known as "the Troubles" until the 1998 Good Friday Agreement brought relative peace.
